 "_": "A core selector on a chordal graph, the k-th power of a path on n vertices (n = 12, k = 6): every clique lies in a window of 7 consecutive vertices. The checker verifies the elimination ordering, DERIVES the maximal bags, and checks every core of size 5 -- not a list someone wrote. One step finds a core omitting at most 2 core vertices for every exterior vertex; another shows NO core does better than 2; a reduction lets the adversary be the two simplicial ends of the path only, checked edge by edge. `certo compose examples/construction_core_selector.json`.",
